60
00:36:42.000 --> 00:37:14.000
making coffee in the morning or shampooing your hair, flossing your teeth, hand sanitizing if you're a caregiver in a hospital. These are the kinds of things that do seem to be where it is possible to really habituate it and have it for the most part continue. But I think most things require, most of the things we care about in life. And also you can put on autopilot, right, your retirement savings. So there are some magic exceptions. but I do think a lot of the goals we have in life,
比如早上煮咖啡、洗头发、用牙线剔牙，或者如果你是医院的医护人员，进行手部消毒。这些似乎是确实有可能真正养成习惯并在大多数情况下持续下去的事情。但我认为大多数事情都需要，我们需要关心生活中的大多数事情。而且你也可以把退休储蓄置于自动驾驶状态，对吧？所以有一些神奇的例外，但我确实认为我们在生活中拥有的许多目标，

61
00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:41.000
a lot of the things that require effort and thought and deliberation, it's going to be very hard to autopilot them. I'm not sure it's possible. And instead, what I have come to appreciate as the right path to change is to create structures and strategies that you're okay relying on to help you get through the barriers just permanently, right? So, for instance, I still temptation bundled to go to the gym. And that works for me.
许多需要付出努力、思考和深思熟虑的事情，要让它们进入自动驾驶状态是非常困难的。我不确定这是否可能。相反，我逐渐认识到通往改变的正确途径是创建结构和策略，你可以依靠这些策略来帮助你永远克服这些障碍，对吧？例如，我仍然用“诱惑捆绑”法去健身房。这对我很有用。

62
00:37:41.000 --> 00:38:20.000
well, during COVID, I haven't been going to a gym, but to get my exercise in, I look for ways to do that and always will. And I don't feel like I needed to ever end that, that strategy, right? So some of the, I'll call them crutches that we can use to get ourselves to succeed, like accountability or temptation bundling, as we've talked about, there's no need to set them aside. There's no need to say, I'm going to use this for a month. And then I'll be off to the races and I won't need this tactic anymore. Instead, I think we should expect to use them forever and not see that as a downside. It's just that's, you know, we need these tools to achieve our goals and we should keep using them. And that's how we get where we want to be.
嗯，在新冠疫情期间，我一直没去健身房，但为了锻炼身体，我一直在寻找方法，而且以后也会一直这样。我觉得我不需要结束那个策略，对吧？所以有些我称之为“拐杖”的东西，我们可以用它们来促使自己成功，比如我们讨论过的责任感或诱惑捆绑法，没有必要把它们放在一边。没有必要说，我要用这个一个月，然后我就会一飞冲天，再也不需要这个战术了。相反，我认为我们应该指望永远使用它们，并且不要将其视为缺点。这只是，你知道的，我们需要这些工具来达到我们的目标，我们应该继续使用它们。这就是我们如何到达我们想去的地方。

